{"title":"Two Tangent Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The two tangent theorem states that given a circle, if P is any point lying outside the circle, and if A and B are points such that PA and PB are tangent to the circle, then PA = PB.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proofs\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proofs</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Proof_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_Tangent_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Twotangenttheorem.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/57/Twotangenttheorem.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"777\" height=\"477\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proofs\">Proofs</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_Tangent_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proofs\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_1\">Proof 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_Tangent_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03ea4d2f1aeb81b1772b0c2cdd2625c05dd41ac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OBP$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c20f306e46f7431949fe9c321a5e286555e867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OAP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> are both right triangles with two equal sides, the third sides are both equal.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_2\">Proof 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_Tangent_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>From a simple application of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_of_a_Point_Theorem\" title=\"Power of a Point Theorem\">Power of a Point Theorem</a>, the result follows.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_Tangent_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>2007 AIME II #9</b>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9</a>\n</p><p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is given with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be16c8d07c30f5440b80149ffaae9f6d68636a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=63$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d135a3c557ff830beab63bbb466019bc9c7143d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=448.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/3/0c387397862be18d18896b70dadd7bcb64fe4b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=CF=84.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"126\" height=\"13\" /> The inscribed circle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4050342f16694c6946c030b5d594bdcf7aad34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/ede78a06018011f48c24a76284afce482ebc6c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> and the inscribed circle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b727b773d199f4fa0d684957a720f9c3e9750c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87c4a62f9a706a945d6b32977ae728d692311687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><b>2004 AMC 12A #18</b>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18?srsltid=AfmBOorUkW3ONFcgVgUbr_T95JrEL_71l8VehAsc0vCp-6GurD4BIYYv\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18?srsltid=AfmBOorUkW3ONFcgVgUbr_T95JrEL_71l8VehAsc0vCp-6GurD4BIYYv</a>\n</p><p>Square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. A semicircle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is constructed inside the square, and the tangent to the semicircle from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> intersects side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. What is the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95eaca439ccbf2863a43b05f4de566ccdabdc392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CE}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_Tangent_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Two_Tangent_Theorem&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017145458\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node 